usage: aiwork [-h] [--version] [--config CONFIG]
              {project,hierarchy,draft,campaign,campaign-recover,native,doctor,models,harnesses,context-plan,local-calibrate,tools,a100,benchmark,workflow,plan,patch,self,task,worker,runs,control}
              ...

Run and independently verify engineering jobs.

positional arguments:
  {project,hierarchy,draft,campaign,campaign-recover,native,doctor,models,harnesses,context-plan,local-calibrate,tools,a100,benchmark,workflow,plan,patch,self,task,worker,runs,control}
    project             index repositories and retrieve scoped context or
                        evidence
    hierarchy           register and run reviewed, nested engineering plans
    draft               propose an execution policy for operator review
    campaign            dispatch an authorized self-authored REA-Next fixture
    campaign-recover    verify a reconstruction from static evidence
    native              reconstruct or independently grade an authorized
                        native target
    doctor              show Python, GPU and executable inventory
    models              discover configured endpoints and model inventory
    harnesses           show harness executable inventory
    context-plan        plan bounded context from measurements; no inference
                        or service changes
    local-calibrate     bounded private Ollama calibration; dry run unless
                        --apply
    tools               list built-in tools and configured specialist adapters
    a100                inspect SSH and manage scoped Lambda lifecycle
    benchmark           compare explicit profiles on frozen engineering
                        fixtures
    workflow            run or resume a deterministic dependency graph
    plan                plan, run and integrate an engineering objective
    patch               inspect the verified patch and optionally check a Git
                        checkout
    self                propose a read-only index improvement from a committed
                        checkout
    task                submit, inspect, or resume a job
    worker              consume the persistent queue
    runs                list jobs or inspect one job
    control             pause new work or resume queue dispatch

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --version             show program's version number and exit
  --config CONFIG       operator TOML file, defaults to aiwork.local.toml
